.Dt CHMOD 1
.Os Project9
.Sh NAME
.Nm chmod
.Nd change file permissions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar octal-mode file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sets the mode of each file.
The three low octal digits give permissions for owner, group and other.
Each digit is the sum of 4 for read, 2 for write and 1 for execute or search.
The owner or root may set the mode.
On directories, 1000 enables sticky removal checks and 2000 makes new
entries inherit the directory's group.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr chown 1 ,
.Xr umask 1 ,
.Xr statx 2
